  "title": "Trump's Mail-In Voting Rejection and Court Challenges",
  "summary": "The US Supreme Court has upheld its decision to allow mail-in voting in midterms, following a federal judge's earlier decision to block new limits. President Trump faces legal challenges over his administration's stance on mail-in voting, as the court continues to oppose restrictions on the process.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "The US Supreme Court has renewed its appeal to allow restrictions on mail-in voting in November’s midterm elections.",
      "confidence": 0.95
